Root cause:
The bug was introduced in a previous commit (9683efc4) that likely altered the handling of audio frames, specifically the management of presentation timestamps (PTS) and the deletion of DTS (decoding timestamps). The patch addresses the absence of proper PTS handling for audio frames, which was causing audio playback issues. The modifications ensure that PTS values are correctly set and updated based on the current frame duration, thereby fixing the audio synchronization problem.
